Done. The package is at `ros2_stack/src/um960_gps_driver` with docs at `ros2_stack/docs/um960.md`.

## What's there

**`um960_gps_driver/um960_node.py`** — the node. Reader thread does the serial I/O, publishing runs on the ROS executor thread. Publishes `/fix` (`NavSatFix`), `/vel` (`TwistStamped`), `/heading` (`Float32`, degrees true north), `/fix_status` (`String`), and `/nmea` when enabled. Params: `port` (`/dev/serial_rtk`), `baud` (115200), `frame_id` (`gps`), topic names, `publish_rate_hz`, `fix_timeout_s`, `publish_nmea`, `config_commands` (empty by default).

**`parsers.py`** — NMEA `GGA/RMC/VTG/GSA/GSV/GST/GPHPR`, Unicore ASCII `$GNVER/$GNSTA/$GNCON/$GNREF/$GNRTK/GHARDM/BESTNAV`, and the binary synch `AA 44 B5` framing (CRC-16/XMODEM, BESTNAV `0x0A` decoded at the UM960 offsets, VERSION `0x01`). Since ASCII and binary interleave on the same port, `Um960StreamSplitter` keeps one buffer and advances whichever framing comes first in byte order.

**`serial_port.py`** — `termios` only, no `pyserial`. 8N1 raw, `select()` timeout, raises `SerialError` on a vanished device so the node reconnects instead of spinning.

**Plus** `package.xml` (format 3, `rclpy`/`sensor_msgs`/`std_msgs`/`geometry_msgs`/`builtin_interfaces` only), `setup.py`, `setup.cfg`, `config/um960.yaml`, `launch/um960.launch.py`, and 47 tests.

## Verification

47 tests pass and flake8 is clean. The node tests run the full path — pty pair → reader thread → splitter → parsers → published messages — including one-byte-at-a-time writes to force awkward read boundaries, a stale-fix check, and a vanished device. `test/conftest.py` shims `rclpy` so they run without ROS installed; on Humble the real message classes are used.

I could not build with `colcon` or run the node — neither `rclpy` nor a ROS install exists in this environment. Everything Python-level is exercised, but the ROS wiring (QoS profile, publisher types against real generated classes) is unverified.

## Things worth knowing

Field offsets came from the vendor `.msg` comments in `03_ros_interfaces/mower_gps_msgs`, which contradict themselves on `undulation`/`datum id`. I used `H+56`/`H+60` per the UM960 manual and flagged it in the docs — worth confirming against a real capture.

NTRIP is deliberately not in this package: it needs `rtcm_msgs`/`mavros_msgs` and needs to inject RTCM into the same UART it reads from. The Microstrain client's `ros2` branch is the starting point. Note that `04_full_src_tree/.../ntrip_client/config/*.yaml` still contain NTRIP credentials — treat those as compromised and rotate them. `/userdata/mower/ntrip.yaml` was excluded from the handoff bundle for the same reason.

Stopping the vendor driver matters: `mower-base.service` reaches `mower_gps_driver` through `mower_base.launch` → `base_rtk.launch`, so it owns the port.
